### Dynamic Index Example  
#### Dynamically index string fields as the autocomplete type.  
The following index definition for the `sample_mflix.movies` collection in the [sample dataset](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/sample-data/#std-label-available-sample-datasets) indexes all string fields at the root-level in the documents in the collection as the `autocomplete` type with default settings. It also excludes string fields like `poster`, `languages`, `rated`, `lastupdated`, `fullplot`, and `awards` from being indexed.  
**Note:**  
To configure `typeSet` using the Atlas Administration API for dynamic mappings, you must use API (Application Programming Interface) version 2025-09-10 or higher.  
```json
{
"mappings": {
"dynamic": {
"typeSet": "moviesStringIndex"
},
"fields": {
"poster": [],
"languages": [],
"rated": [],
"lastupdated": [],
"fullplot": [],
"awards": []
}
},
"typeSets": [
{
"name": "moviesStringIndex",
"types": [
{
"type": "autocomplete"
}
]
}
]
}
```

### Multiple Types Example  
#### Index specific field as autocomplete and string types.  
The following index definition example uses the `sample_mflix.movies` collection to index a field as multiple types. The following index definition indexes the `title` field as the following types:  
- `autocomplete` type to support autocompletion for queries using the [autocomplete](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/autocomplete#std-label-autocomplete-ref) operator.  
- `string` type to support text search using operators such [text](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/text#std-label-text-ref), [phrase](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/phrase#std-label-phrase-ref), and so on.  
```json
curl --header "Authorization: Bearer ${ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
--header "Accept: application/vnd.atlas.2025-03-12+json" \
--header "Content-Type: application/json" \
-X POST "https://cloud.mongodb.com/api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/search/indexes" \
-d '{ "collectionName": "movies",
"database": "sample_mflix",
"name": "default",
"type": "search",
"definition": {
"mappings": {
"dynamic": false,
"fields": {
"title": [
{
"type": "autocomplete",
"analyzer": "lucene.standard",
"tokenization": "edgeGram",
"minGrams": 2,
"maxGrams": 15,
"foldDiacritics": false
},
{
"type": "string"
}
]
}
}
}
}'
```

### Try an Example for the `autocomplete` Type  
The following index definition examples use collections in the [sample data](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/sample-data/#std-label-available-sample-datasets). After you [load the sample data](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/import/load-sample-data/#std-label-load-sample-data), you can use these examples to index fields as the `autocomplete` type.  
To learn how to set up and run the following example code, see [Define the Index for the token Type](/docs/search/index/field-types/token-type#std-label-define-index-token-admin-api).  
#### Basic Example  
##### Index specific field using static mappings as autocomplete type.  
The following index definition example uses the `sample_mflix.movies` collection. The index definition indexes only the `title` field as the `autocomplete` type to support search-as-you-type queries against that field using the [autocomplete](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/autocomplete#std-label-autocomplete-ref) operator. The index definition also specifies the following:  
- Use the [standard](/docs/search/index/analyzers/standard#std-label-ref-standard-analyzer) analyzer to divide text values into terms based on word boundaries.  
- Use the `edgeGram` tokenization strategy to index characters starting at the left side of the words .  
- Index a minimum of `3` characters per indexed sequence.  
- Index a maximum of `5` characters per indexed sequence.  
- Include diacritic marks in the index and query text.  
- Use the `stableTfl` [similarity algorithm](/docs/search/query/score/get-details#std-label-fts-similarity-algorithms) to ensure consistent document scoring across all search nodes and replica set members.  
```bash
{
"mappings": {
"dynamic": false,
"fields": {
"title": {
"type": "autocomplete",
"analyzer": "lucene.standard",
"tokenization": "edgeGram",
"minGrams": 3,
"maxGrams": 5,
"foldDiacritics": false,
"similarity": { "type": "stableTfl" }
}
}
}
```  
