## Define the Index for the `document` Type  
1. Retrieve your Service Account access token for the project.  
Use your service account to generate an access token, which authenticates your requests to the Atlas Administration API. To learn how to generate an access token, see [Make an API (Application Programming Interface) Request.](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/configure-api-access/#std-label-example-api-request)  
2. Make an API (Application Programming Interface) call.  
Replace the following values in the `curl` command below. This command sends a `POST` request to your cluster to create a MongoDB Search index with the `document` field type.  
- Replace \{`ACCESS-TOKEN`} with the output from the preceding step  
- Replace \{`groupId`} with the project ID of the project where you want to create the MongoDB Search index  
- Replace \{`clusterName`} with the name of the cluster where you want to create the MongoDB Search index  
```shell
curl --header "Authorization: Bearer ${ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
--header "Accept: application/vnd.atlas.2025-03-12+json" \
--header "Content-Type: application/json" \
-X POST "https://cloud.mongodb.com/api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/search/indexes" \
-d '{ "collectionName": "<collection>",
"database": "<database>",
"name": "default",
"type": "search",
"definition": {
"mappings": {
"dynamic": true|false | {
"typeSet": "<type-set-name>"
},
"fields": {
"<field-name>": {
"type": "document",
"dynamic": true|false,
"fields": {
"<sub-field-name>": {
<field-mapping-definition>
},
...
}
},
...
}
},
"typeSets": [
{
"name": <type-set-name>",
"types": [
{
"type": "<field-type>",
...
},
...
]
}
]
}
}'

```

### Index Dynamically Using Default typeSet  
#### Enables dynamic mappings to index all dynamically indexable field types.  
The following index definition for the `sample_mflix.movies` collection indexes the `awards` field as the `document` type. It also configures MongoDB Search to automatically index all the dynamically indexable fields inside the `awards` object.  
```shell
curl --header "Authorization: Bearer ${ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
--header "Accept: application/vnd.atlas.2025-03-12+json" \
--header "Content-Type: application/json" \
-X POST "https://cloud.mongodb.com/api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/search/indexes" \
-d '{ "collectionName": "movies",
"database": "sample_mflix",
"name": "default",
"type": "search",
"definition": {
"mappings": {
"dynamic": false,
"fields": {
"awards": {
"type": "document",
"dynamic": true
}
}
}
}
}'
```

### Index Dynamically Using Configured typeSet  
#### Configures field types to dynamically index.  
The following index definition for the `sample_mflix.movies` collection indexes the `awards` field as the `document` type. It references the `typeSet` name, `onlyNumbers`. The field type definition named `onlyNumbers` enables automatic indexing for only fields of type `number` in the `awards` document.  
**Note:**  
To configure `typeSet` using the Atlas Administration API for dynamic mappings, you must use API (Application Programming Interface) version 2025-09-10 or higher.  
```shell
curl --header "Authorization: Bearer ${ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
--header "Accept: application/vnd.atlas.2025-03-12+json" \
--header "Content-Type: application/json" \
-X POST "https://cloud.mongodb.com/api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/search/indexes" \
-d '{ "collectionName": "movies",
"database": "sample_mflix",
"name": "default",
"type": "search",
"definition": {
"mappings": {
"dynamic": false,
"fields": {
"awards": {
"type": "document",
"dynamic": {
"typeSet": "onlyNumbers"
}
}
}
},
"typeSets": [
{
"name": "onlyNumbers",
"types": [
{
"type": "number"
}
]
}
]
}
}'
```  
You can use the MongoDB Search `document` type to index fields in objects or documents.  
If you enable [dynamic mappings](/docs/search/index/define-field-mappings#std-label-static-dynamic-mappings), MongoDB Search automatically indexes all dynamically indexable fields types in a `document` type field. Alternatively, you can configure dynamic mappings to index only specific field types nested in a `document` type field.  
You can use the **Visual Editor** or the  **JSON Editor** in the Atlas UI, Atlas CLI, Atlas Administration API, [`mongosh`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongodb-shell/#mongodb-binary-bin.mongosh), MongoDB Compass, or MongoDB drivers to index fields as the `document` type.

