### Dynamic Index Examples  
#### Combine dynamic mappings with static mappings to index nested fields as different field types.  
#### Enable Dynamic Indexing  
The following index definition for the `sample_training.companies` namespace configures MongoDB Search to automatically index all dynamically indexable fields inside the objects in the `products` array. It also configures the `category_code` field to be indexed as the [token](/docs/search/index/field-types/token-type#std-label-bson-data-types-token) type, which is not included in the default type set for dynamic mappings, to support MongoDB Search [`facet` (MongoDB Search Operator)](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/facet#std-label-fts-facet-ref) queries against that field.  
```python
