You can use the MongoDB Search `objectId` type to index [ObjectId](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/bson-types/#objectid) values. You can query fields of type `objectId` using the [equals](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/equals#std-label-equals-ref) and [in](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/in#std-label-in-ref) operators.  
You can also use the `objectId` type to index:  
- Fields whose value is an array of `objectId`. To learn more, see [How to Index the Elements of an Array.](/docs/search/index/field-types/array-type#std-label-fts-array-ref)  
- `objectId` fields inside an array of documents indexed as the [embeddedDocuments](/docs/search/index/field-types/embedded-documents-type#std-label-bson-data-types-embedded-documents) type.  
To facet on `objectId` values, use [MongoDB View](/docs/search/about/view-support#std-label-fts-transform-documents-collections) to convert the value to `string` type. For a demonstration of transforming an `objectId` type to `string` type for faceting, see [Transform Fields for Faceting.](/docs/search/about/view-support#std-label-fts-transform-for-facet)  
If you enable [dynamic mappings](/docs/search/index/define-field-mappings#std-label-static-dynamic-mappings), MongoDB Search automatically indexes fields of type `objectId`. You can use the **Visual Editor** or the  **JSON Editor** in the Atlas UI to index fields as the `objectId` type.

