## Define the Index for the [stringFacet](/docs/search/index/field-types/string-facet-type#std-label-bson-data-types-string-facet) Type  
To define the index for the `stringFacet` type, choose your preferred configuration method in the Atlas UI and then select the database and collection.  
1. Click Refine Your Index to configure your index.  
2. In the Field Mappings section, click Add Field
Mapping to open the Add Field Mapping window.  
3. Click Customized Configuration.  
4. Select the field to index from the Field Name dropdown.  
**Note:**  
You can't index fields that contain the dollar (`$`) sign at the start of the field name.  
5. Click the Data Type dropdown and select StringFacet. To learn more more about this type, see [Field Properties](/docs/search/index/field-types/string-facet-type#std-label-fts-field-types-string-facet-options).  
6. Click Add.  
The following is the JSON (Javascript Object Notation) syntax for the `stringFacet` type. Replace the default index definition with the following. To learn more about the fields, see [Field Properties](/docs/search/index/field-types/vector-type#std-label-fts-vector-field-type-properties).  
```json
{
"mappings": {
"dynamic": true|false,
"fields": {
"<field-name>": {
"type": "stringFacet"
}
}
}
}
```

### stringFacet Type Example  
The following index definition for the `sample_mflix.movies` collection in the [sample dataset](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/sample-data/#std-label-available-sample-datasets) indexes the `genres` field as `stringFacet` for faceting.  
In the Add Field Mapping window, select genres from the Field
Name dropdown.  
Click the Data Type dropdown and select StringFacet.  
Click Add.  
```json
{
"mappings": {
"dynamic": false,
"fields": {
"genres": {
"type": "stringFacet"
}
}
}
}
```

### Multiple Types Example  
The following index definition for the `sample_mflix.movies` collection in the [sample dataset](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/sample-data/#std-label-available-sample-datasets) indexes the `genres` field as `stringFacet` and `string` types to return the following types of results for your queries:  
- Metadata results for queries using MongoDB Search [`facet` (MongoDB Search Operator).](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/facet#std-label-fts-facet-ref)  
- Search results for queries using MongoDB Search operators like [text](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/text#std-label-text-ref), [phrase](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/phrase#std-label-phrase-ref), and other operators that perform text search.  
