## Create a MongoDB Search Index  
To create a MongoDB Search index using the Atlas Administration API:  
1. Send a `POST` request.  
Send a `POST` request to the `search/indexes` [endpoint.](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-creategroupclustersearchindex)  
**Note:**  
This `curl` command uses a service account access token ([OAuth 2.0](https://oauth.net/2/)) to authenticate instead of API keys. To learn more, see [Get Started with the Atlas Administration API.](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/configure-api-access/#std-label-atlas-admin-api-access)  
```sh
curl --header "Authorization: Bearer {ACCESS-TOKEN}" \
--header "Accept: application/json" \
--header "Content-Type: application/json" \
--include \
--request POST "https://cloud.mongodb.com/api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/search/indexes" \
--data '
{
"collectionName": "<collection-name>",
"database": "<database-name>",
"name": "<index-name>",
"type": "search",
"definition":
{
"analyzer": "<analyzer-name>",
"searchAnalyzer": "<analyzer-name>",
"mappings": {
"dynamic": <boolean>,
"fields": { <field-definition> }
},
"numPartitions": <integer>,
"analyzers": [ {
<custom-analyzer-definition>
}
],
"storedSource": <boolean> | {
<stored-source-definition>
},
"synonyms": [
{
<synonym-mapping-definition>
}
]
}
}'
```  
To learn more about the syntax and parameters for this endpoint, see [Create One.](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-creategroupclustersearchindex)  
2. Review the response.  
IMPORTANT: Atlas doesn't create the index if the collection doesn't exist, but it still returns a `200` status.

## Edit a MongoDB Search Index  
To edit a MongoDB Search index using the Atlas Administration API:  
1. Send a `PATCH` request.  
Send a `PATCH` request with either the unique ID or name of the MongoDB Search index that you wish to modify to the `search/indexes/` endpoint.  
**Note:**  
This `curl` command uses a service account access token ([OAuth 2.0](https://oauth.net/2/)) to authenticate instead of API keys. To learn more, see [Get Started with the Atlas Administration API.](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/configure-api-access/#std-label-atlas-admin-api-access)  
```sh
curl --header "Authorization: Bearer {ACCESS-TOKEN}" \
--header "Accept: application/json" \
--header "Content-Type: application/json" \
--include \
--request PATCH "https://cloud.mongodb.com/api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/search/indexes/{indexId}" \
--data '
{
"definition":
{
"analyzer": "lucene.<analyzer>",
"analyzers": [
{
"charFilters": [ ... ],
"name": "string",
"tokenFilters": [ ... ],
"tokenizer": { ... }
}
],
"mappings": {
"dynamic": true | false,
"fields": {
"property1": {},
...
}
},
"searchAnalyzer": "<analyzer-name>",
"storedSource": {
"include | exclude": [...]
},
"synonyms": [
{
<synonym-mapping-definition>
}
}
]
}
}'
```  
To learn more about the syntax and parameters for either endpoint, see [Update One By Name](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-updategroupclustersearchindexbyname) and [Update One By ID.](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/api/doc/atlas-admin-api-v2/operation/operation-updategroupclustersearchindex)  
2. Review the response.  
**Note:**  
While your updated index is building, different nodes might update at varying speeds. During this period, you might experience mixed query results, reflecting both the new index definition and the previous index definition.

### Example  
The following example shows you how to use the `atlas clusters` command to create a MongoDB Search index in non-interactive mode with a configuration file.  
1. Create an `indexDef.json` configuration file.  
```json
{
"collectionName": "movies",
"database": "sample_mflix",
"definition": {
"mappings": {
"dynamic": true
},
},
"name": "searchIndex"
}
```  
2. Create a MongoDB Search index.  
Specify the cluster name and run the following command:  
```sh
atlas clusters search indexes create --file indexDef.json --clusterName <clusterName>
```

