## Delete a MongoDB Search Index  
**Warning: Deleting Search Indexes and Clusters Is Irreversible**  
Deleting Search indexes and associated clusters is a permanent action. MongoDB doesn't provide support for recovering deleted Search indexes or data. Ensure that you have taken appropriate measures, such as creating backups, to avoid data loss before proceeding.  
MongoDB doesn't support requests to recover deleted Search indexes or data. You are responsible for data integrity and configurations.  
To delete a MongoDB Search index on a collection using the [Java Driver](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/java/sync/current/indexes/#atlas-search-indexes), use the `dropSearchIndex()` method:  
1. Create a new file named `DeleteIndex.java`.  
2. Copy the following code example into the file.  
The following sample application deletes the specified MongoDB Search index on the specified collection.  
```java
