## Edit a MongoDB Search Index  
To edit a MongoDB Search index using the [Java Driver:](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/java/sync/current/)  
1. Create a new file named `EditIndex.java`.  
2. Copy the following code example into the file.  
```java
import com.mongodb.client.MongoClient;
import com.mongodb.client.MongoClients;
import com.mongodb.client.MongoCollection;
import com.mongodb.client.MongoDatabase;
import org.bson.Document;

public class EditIndex {
public static void main(String[] args) {
// connect to your Atlas cluster
String uri = "<connection-string>";

try (MongoClient mongoClient = MongoClients.create(uri)) {
// set namespace
MongoDatabase database = mongoClient.getDatabase("<document-name>");
MongoCollection<Document> collection = database.getCollection("<collection-name>");
// define field mappings
Document index = new Document("analyzer", "<analyzer-name>").append(
"mappings", new Document("dynamic", <true|false>)
.append("fields", new Document("<field-name>",
new Document("type", "<field-type>"))));
// run the updateSearchIndex() method
collection.updateSearchIndex("<index-name>", index);
}
}
}

```  
3. Replace the following values in the code and then save the file.  
- `<connection-string>` - Your Atlas connection string. To learn more, see [Connect to a Cluster via Client Libraries.](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/driver-connection/#std-label-connect-via-driver)  
IMPORTANT: In your connection string, don't include the [Write Concern](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/write-concern/#std-label-write-concern) setting.  
- `<database-name>` - The name of the database that contains the collection.  
- `<collection-name>` - The name of the collection for which you want to retrieve the index.  
- `<analyzer-name>` - The name of the [analyzer.](/docs/search/index/analyzers/overview#std-label-analyzers-ref)  
- `dynamic` - The flag that indicates whether or not to [automatically](/docs/search/index/define-field-mappings#std-label-static-dynamic-mappings) index the fields.  
- `<field-name>` - The name of the field to index.  
- `<field-type>` - The field data [type.](/docs/search/index/define-field-mappings#std-label-bson-data-types)  
- `<index-name>` - The name of the index.  
4. Compile and run the file.  
```shell
javac EditIndex.java
java EditIndex
```  
The `updateSearchIndex()` method runs asynchronously. Use the `listSearchIndexes()` method to determine if the changes have been applied to your index. To learn more about retrieving MongoDB Search indexes, see [Manage MongoDB Search Indexes.](/docs/search/index/manage-indexes#std-label-ref-view-index-programmatically)  
**See also:**  
[MongoDB Search Indexes](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/java/sync/current/indexes/#atlas-search-indexes)  
**Note:**  
While your updated index is building, different nodes might update at varying speeds. During this period, you might experience mixed query results, reflecting both the new index definition and the previous index definition.

