In the Stored Source Fields section, click All Except Specified.  
Select `directors` from the dropdown in the Field Name column and click Add.  
Click Add Field to specify another field to exclude.  
Select `imdb.rating` from the dropdown in the Field Name column and click Add.  
Click Save Changes.  
The following example stores all fields except `directors` and `imdb.rating` in the documents in the collection. After you select your preferred configuration method, select the `movies` collection under the `sample_mflix` database.  
Append lines 5 to 10 from the following example to the index definition to exclude the specified fields. The example uses the [dot notation](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/document/#std-label-document-dot-notation) to specify nested fields.  
