### Query for Matching Embedded Documents Only  
The following query returns only the nested documents that match the query. The query uses MongoDB Search [compound operator](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/compound#std-label-compound-ref) clauses in the [`$search`](/docs/search/query/aggregation-stages/search#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-search) stage to find matching documents and then the [aggregation operators](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/mql/expressions/#std-label-aggregation-expressions) in the [`$project`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/project/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-project) stage to return only matching embedded documents. Specifically, the query specifies the following pipeline stages:  
| [`$search`](/docs/search/query/aggregation-stages/search#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-search) | Specifies the following criteria in the [compound operator](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/compound#std-label-compound-ref) `must` clause: Check if `items.price` field exists in the collection.; Search for the items tagged as `school` in the `items.tags` field.; Match only if value is more than 2 for the `items.quantity` field. |
| --- | --- |
| [`$limit`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/limit/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-limit) | Limits the output to `5` documents. |
| [`$project`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/project/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-project) | Perform the following actions: Exclude the `_id` field and only include the `items` and `storeLocation` fields.; Use [`$filter`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/filter/#mongodb-expression-exp.-filter) to return only elements of the `items` input array that match the condition specified using the [`$and`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/and/#mongodb-expression-exp.-and) operator. The `and` operator uses the following operators:[`$ifNull`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/ifNull/#mongodb-expression-exp.-ifNull) to determine if `items.price` contains null values and replace null values, if present, with the replacement expression `false`.; [`$gt`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/gt/#mongodb-expression-exp.-gt) to check if quantity is greater than 2.; [`$in`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/in/#mongodb-expression-exp.-in) to check if `office` exists in the `tags` array. |  
```json
db.sales.aggregate(
{
"$search": {
"embeddedDocument": {
"path": "items",
"operator": {
"compound": {
"must": [
{
"range": {
"path": "items.quantity",
"gt": 2
}
},
{
"exists": {
"path": "items.price"
}
},
{
"text": {
"path": "items.tags",
"query": "school"
}
}
]
}
}
}
}
},
{
"$limit": 2
},
{
"$project": {
"_id": 0,
"storeLocation": 1,
"items": {
"$filter": {
"input": "$items",
"cond": {
"$and": [
{
"$ifNull": [
"$$this.price", "false"
]
},
{
"$gt": [
"$$this.quantity", 2
]
},
{
"$in": [
"office", "$$this.tags"
]
}
]
}
}
}
}
}
)
```  
