## Syntax  
`hasRoot` has the following syntax:  
```javascript
{
$search: {
"index": "<index name>", // optional, defaults to "default"
"hasRoot": {
"operator": {
<operator-specification>
}
},
"returnScope": {
"path": "<embedded-documents-field-to-retrieve>"
},
"returnStoredSource": true,
}
}
```

### Sample Index  
The queries in this section use the following index. This index definition configures MongoDB Search to do the following:  
- Automatically index all the dynamically indexable fields in the collection.  
- Index the `products`, `funding_rounds`, and `funding_rounds.investments` fields as the [embeddedDocuments](/docs/search/index/field-types/embedded-documents-type#std-label-bson-data-types-embedded-documents) type.  
- Store the following fields on `mongot`:  
- `funding_rounds.raised_currency_code`  
- `funding_rounds.raised_amount`  
- `funding_rounds.investments`  
- `products.name`  
```json
{
"mappings": {
"dynamic": true,
"fields": {
"funding_rounds": {
"dynamic": true,
"fields": {
"investments": [
{
"dynamic": true,
"type": "embeddedDocuments"
}
]
},
"storedSource": {
"include": [
"raised_currency_code",
"raised_amount",
"investments"
]
},
"type": "embeddedDocuments"
},
"products": {
"dynamic": true,
"storedSource": {
"include": [
"name"
]
},
"type": "embeddedDocuments"
}
}
}
}
```

