### Example 3: Multiple Analyzers  
The following example uses `find()` to identify input documents, and then uses a `moreLikeThis` operator to find similar documents. For this example, the index definition uses [static mappings](/docs/search/index/define-field-mappings#std-label-static-dynamic-mappings) to index the fields in the `sample_mflix.movies` collection with different analyzers. The index definition:  
- Configures an index on the `_id`, `title` and `genres` fields.  
- Analyzes the `title` field using the `lucene.standard` analyzer and an alternate analyzer named `keywordAnalyzer` that uses the `lucene.keyword` analyzer.  
- Analyzes and searches the fields using the `lucene.english` analyzer.  
```javascript
