"dynamic": false,
"fields": {
"title": {
"type": "string",
"analyzer": "lucene.standard",
"multi": {
"keywordAnalyzer": {
"type": "string",
"analyzer": "lucene.keyword"
}
}
},
"genres": {
"type": "string"
},
"_id": {
"type": "objectId"
}
}
},
"analyzer": "lucene.english"
}
```  
**Example:**  
The following `find()` query retrieves the movies with the title "Alice in Wonderland" and stores the results in `movie`. It specifies that the results should only contain the `title` and `genres` fields for the matching documents. Note that, by default, the `find()` command always returns the `_id` field, the value for which might be different on your cluster.  
