#### Group Children by Parent  
##### Group children by parent using the searchRootDocumentId meta field.  
The following query uses the [`range` (MongoDB Search Operator)](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/range#std-label-range-ref) to query the `funding_rounds.raised_amount` field for amount greater than and equal to `5000000` and less than and equal to `10000000`. It sets the query scope as `funding_rounds` field using the `returnScope` option. It groups the matching `funding_rounds` under each parent company by using the `searchRootDocumentId` meta field as the group key and computes the average `raised_amount` per company in the `avgRaisedAmount` field. It sorts the results by `avgRaisedAmount` in descending order and limits the number of results to `10` companies.  
```javascript
db.companies.aggregate([
{
"$search": {
"returnStoredSource": true,
"returnScope": {
"path": "funding_rounds"
},
"range": {
"path": "funding_rounds.raised_amount",
"gte": 5000000,
"lte": 10000000
}
}
},
{
"$group": {
"_id": { "$meta": "searchRootDocumentId" },
"funding_rounds": {
"$push": {
"round_code": "$round_code",
"raised_amount": "$raised_amount",
"raised_currency_code": "$raised_currency_code"
}
},
"avgRaisedAmount": { "$avg": "$raised_amount" }
}
},
{ "$sort": { "avgRaisedAmount": -1 } },
{ "$limit": 10 }
])

```  
