## Normalize the Score  
You can normalize your [`$search`](/docs/search/query/aggregation-stages/search#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-search) query score in the range from `0` to `1` in the subsequent stages of your aggregation pipeline. You can use the following stages after your [`$search`](/docs/search/query/aggregation-stages/search#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-search) stage in the following order to normalize the score:  
- [`$addFields`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/addFields/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-addFields)  
```json
{
"$addFields": {
"score": {
"$meta": "searchScore"
}
}
}
```  
- [`$setWindowFields`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/setWindowFields/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-setWindowFields)  
```json
{
"$setWindowFields": {
"output": {
"maxScore": {
"$max": "$score"
}
}
}
}
```  
- [`$addFields`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/addFields/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-addFields)  
```json
{
"$addFields": {
"normalizedScore": {
"$divide": [
"$score", "$maxScore"
]
}
}
}
```

