## Syntax  
`sort` has the following syntax:  
```json
{
"$search": {
"index": "<index name>", // optional, defaults to "default"
"<operator>": { // such as "text", "compound", or "phrase"
<operator-specification>
},
"sort": {
score: {$meta: "searchScore"}, // optional field
"<field-to-sort>": <sort-order>, // 1 or -1, or a document
...
}
}
}
```  
| Parameter | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `score` | Optional. Determines whether to sort by the search score. To learn more, see [Sort by Score And a Unique Field.](/docs/search/query/sort#std-label-fts-sort-score-unique-field) |
| `<field-to-sort>` | Required. The name of the field to sort by. |
| `<sort-order>` | Required. Determines the sort order. Use `1` for ascending order and `-1` for descending order. If you want to specify the [noData](/docs/search/query/sort#std-label-fts-sort-null) field, use a document with the following syntax: `"<field-to-sort>": {
order: 1 | -1, // required field
noData: "lowest" | "highest" // optional field
},
...` |

### Index Definition  
The example queries in this page use either the `sample_mflix.movies`, the `sample_airbnb.listingsAndReview`, or a custom collection. If you create the following indexes on these collections, you can run the sample queries against the indexed fields.  
#### movies Collection  
The index definition for the `movies` collection specifies the following:  
- Index `awards.wins` field as:  
- `number` type for sorting and querying, including running [`facet` (MongoDB Search Operator)](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/facet#std-label-fts-facet-ref) queries  
- Index `released` field as:  
- `date` type for sorting and querying, including running [`facet` (MongoDB Search Operator)](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/facet#std-label-fts-facet-ref) queries  
- Index `title` field as:  
- `token` type for sorting  
- `string` type for querying  
```json
{
"mappings": {
"dynamic": true,
"fields": {
"awards": {
"dynamic": false,
"fields": {
"wins": [
{
"type": "number"
}
]
},
"type": "document"
},
"released": [
{
"type": "date"
}
],
"title": [{
"type": "token"
}, {
"type": "string"
}]
}
}
}
```  
For the preceding index definition, MongoDB Search creates an index named `default` with [static mappings](/docs/search/index/define-field-mappings#std-label-static-dynamic-mappings) on the specified fields.  
#### listingsAndReviews Collection  
The example queries against the `sample_airbnb.listingsAndReviews` collection use the following index. The index definition specifies dynamic mappings on the fields in the collection:  
```json
{
"mappings": {
"dynamic": true
}
}
```  
