### Sort by Null Values  
Consider the following queries that search field `b` for the string `hello` in the `users` collection using the [text](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/text#std-label-text-ref) operator. The query then sorts the results by field `c`, which contains null or missing values for some documents in the collection.  
To learn more, see [Sort by Null and Missing Values.](/docs/search/query/sort#std-label-fts-sort-null)  
#### Ascending Sort (Default)  
During an ascending sort, MongoDB Search returns documents with null or missing values at the top of the results by default, as shown in the following example:  
```json
db.users.aggregate([
{
"$search": {
"text": {
"path": "b",
"query": "hello"
},
"sort": { "c": 1 }
}
},
{
"$project": {
"_id": 1,
"c": 1,
"score": { "$meta": "searchScore" }
}
}
])
```  
**Output:**  
```js
