score: 0.025981096550822258
},
{ _id: 1, c: true, score: 0.025981096550822258 }
]
```  
The order of documents with `"_id": 4`, `"_id": 5`, `"_id": 6`, and `"_id": 7` is random because MongoDB Search treats null and missing values as equal when sorting.  
#### Descending Sort (Default)  
For a descending sort, MongoDB Search uses the element with the highest BSON (Binary Javascript Object Notation) type to represent the multi-typed array. MongoDB Search uses `false` to represent the multi-typed array for the document with `_id: 7`, as this is the highest BSON (Binary Javascript Object Notation) type in the array. Since MongoDB Search also ranks `true` values above `false` values, MongoDB Search returns this document after the document with `_id: 1`.

To learn more, see [Sort by Null and Missing Values](/docs/search/query/sort#std-label-fts-sort-null) and [Sort Arrays with Multiple Types.](/docs/search/query/sort#std-label-fts-sort-arrays-multiple-types)  
