1) Run a basic query.

Run a basic `$search` query by using the [text](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/text#std-label-text-ref) operator.

This query has the following search criteria:

- The `plot` field must contain the word `baseball`.

- [`$limit`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/limit/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-limit) and [`$project`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/project/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-project) stages to return only 3 documents and the `title` and `plot` fields.

```javascript
db.movies.aggregate([
{
$search:
{
"text": {
"query": "baseball",
"path": "plot"
}
}
},
{
$limit: 3
},
{
$project: {
"_id": 0,
"title": 1,
"plot": 1
}
}
])
```

