2) Refine your search.

MongoDB Search provides several [operators](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/overview#std-label-fts-operators) that you can use to build complex queries and retrieve more specific results for your use case. Update your `$search` query to use the [compound](/docs/search/query/operators-collectors/compound#std-label-compound-ref) operator to combine multiple operators into a single query.

This query has the following search criteria:

- The `plot` field must contain the word `baseball`.

- The `genres` field must not contain either `Comedy` or `Romance`.

- [`$limit`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/limit/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-limit) and [`$project`](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/project/#mongodb-pipeline-pipe.-project) stages to return only 3 documents and the `title`, `plot`, and `genres` fields.

```javascript
db.movies.aggregate([
{
$search: {
"compound": {
"must": [
{
"text": {
"query": "baseball",
"path": "plot"
}
}
],
"mustNot": [
{
"text": {
"query": ["Comedy", "Romance"],
"path": "genres"
}
}
]
}
}
},
{
$limit: 3
},
{
$project: {
"_id": 0,
